  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1af15679-6a09-455c-b818-e52fcfe0d8d1-image.png\" style=\"width: 254px; height: 163px;\" /></p><p>Using kirchhoff&#39;s law in the circuit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, we get</p><p>Voltage at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>= voltage at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;+ voltage of battery of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;+ potential difference across&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistance&nbsp;-&nbsp;voltage of battery of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math></p><p>Now potential at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;with respect to point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>",
